        <div class="faq-list">
          <details>
            <summary>What is an image size changer?</summary>
            <p>An image size changer is an online tool that adjusts the width and height (pixel dimensions) of a digital image. It enables you to scale photos for web pages, social media, document uploads, or emails without distortion.</p>
          </details>

          <details>
            <summary>How do I resize an image without distorting it?</summary>
            <p>Keep the aspect ratio lock enabled (🔗). When you enter a new width or height, the other dimension automatically recalculates proportionally, ensuring your photo never looks stretched or squashed.</p>
          </details>

          <details>
            <summary>What is the difference between image size and image file size?</summary>
            <p>Image size refers to pixel dimensions (such as 1920 × 1080 px) which describe how wide and tall the image displays on screen. Image file size refers to digital storage weight in Kilobytes (KB) or Megabytes (MB), which affects upload time and download bandwidth.</p>
          </details>

          <details>
            <summary>Are my images uploaded to any server?</summary>
            <p>No. All image resizing, compression, and conversion happens entirely in your web browser using HTML5 Canvas technology. Your files remain on your device and are never transmitted to our servers.</p>
          </details>

          <details>
            <summary>What image formats are supported?</summary>
            <p>You can upload JPG, JPEG, PNG, WebP, GIF, and BMP files. Output files can be exported as JPG, PNG, or WebP.</p>
          </details>
